#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""spp3-brain-daily — the SPP3 lane's producer pass.

Finished ENS program design material only. Distils an explicit allow-list of settled
documents into short markdown captures and lands them in raw/workspaces/spp3/ via
brain-capture (committed on lane/spp3, pushed to the exchange, fenced and merged by the hub).

Rules this script enforces, per the lane contract:
  - idempotent: a source whose DISTILLED body is unchanged produces no capture
  - no secrets: every body is scanned for credential-shaped values and dropped loudly
  - no operational noise: an explicit allow-list, never a directory sweep
  - NEVER applicant identities or evaluation verdicts: those are live ENS committee
    material and do not belong in Sov's brain. Nothing under Accountability-Workspace,
    no .cron-logs, no Notion exports, no per-applicant scoring.
  - bounded: bodies cap at 12KB with a pointer to the full source on this host

Generic by construction: sources are declared in SOURCES, distilled by one shared
builder, so adding a document is a one-line change and no new code.

Run: spp3-brain-daily [--dry] [--preflight]
  --dry        distil and report, capture nothing
  --preflight  render every source against the last captured bytes and say
               whether a change is safe to ship. Reads only.
"""
